The booster catch tower of KRPC.Bridge's conn.tower_site service, as a package of its own.
It used to travel inside GameData/KRPC.Bridge; it is separate so that installing the bridge
does not install the tower's parts.


WHAT THIS PACKAGE SHIPS
-----------------------

    Patches/TowerCatch.cfg       a ModuleManager patch: text written for this project
    Crafts/Tour Catch v5.craft   the tower craft that tower_spawn_v1 puts on the ground
    LICENSE, NOTICE, TowerCatch.version, manifest.json

Nothing else. No model, no texture, no part and no file belonging to any mod or to the game
is in it. The patch makes COPIES of parts that are already installed (ModuleManager's +PART,
under new names, "TG.*"): the copies take their models from the mods and the game they
come from, in the player's own installation, and nothing is redistributed. The craft lists
those parts by name and position.


WHAT IT NEEDS - INSTALLED SEPARATELY, NEVER BUNDLED
---------------------------------------------------

Without any one of them the patch cannot make a part, KSP cannot load the tower craft and a
tower already in a save is removed by the game at load ("missing parts"). Install them
before this package.

    KRPC.Bridge (this repository)
    MIT License. Its KRPC.Bridge.Tower.dll holds the services that put the tower on the
    ground and read it (conn.tower_site, conn.tower). Earlier versions of the bridge carried
    this patch and the craft inside GameData/KRPC.Bridge: with this package, remove them
    (the deployment tool does), never keep both.

    kRPC
    LGPL v3 or later (service/SpaceCenter: GPL v3). https://github.com/krpc/krpc

    ModuleManager
    CC-BY-SA, ialdabaoth and contributors.

    Modular Launch Pads (AlphaMensae)
    CC-BY-NC-SA 4.0. Source of the mast, the base, the top and the truss copies. Its models
    are not redistributed; do not use pictures of its models in advertising without the
    author's permission.

    HullCamera VDS Continued (linuxgurugamer)
    GPL v3. Source of the tower's four cameras.

    Kerbal Space Program expansions, bought from the game's publisher: Breaking Ground
    (the hinges, "hinge_04") and Making History (the tubes around the hinges, "Tube3").
    They cannot be installed by a mod manager: without them the tower does not load.

The game's own parts (launch clamp, battery bank, structural panel) come from the base game.
ReStock, if installed, only changes the model of the clamp.


